Let the embedder present the primary surface itself.

eglSwapBuffers blocks until the whole context's GPU work has drained, not merely
the work targeting the surface being swapped. When something else owns
presentation -- here VPX renders into its own scanout buffers and commits them
through KMS with an IN_FENCE_FD -- that call is pure cost: it presents a surface
nobody reads, and it serialises the frame, because the CPU cannot begin frame
N+1 until frame N's GPU work has finished. Measured on RK3588: 17 ms of a 25 ms
frame, with the GPU idle for the remainder.

This is the bgfx-side counterpart of SDL_KMSDRM_SKIP_EGL_SURFACE, which already
stops SDL owning presentation for the same surface. Runtime rather than compile
time so the first frames, before the embedder's buffers exist, and any fallback
still present normally.

Applies on top of bgfx-kmsdrm-gbm-egl.patch.

--- a/src/glcontext_egl.cpp
+++ b/src/glcontext_egl.cpp
@@ -779,13 +779,28 @@
 		bx::deleteObject(g_allocator, _swapChain);
 	}
 
+	// FORK PATCH (4kp): let the embedder present the primary surface itself.
+	//
+	// eglSwapBuffers blocks until the whole context's GPU work has drained, not merely the work
+	// targeting the surface being swapped. When something else owns presentation -- here, VPX renders
+	// into its own scanout buffers and commits them through KMS with an IN_FENCE_FD -- that call is
+	// pure cost: it presents a surface nobody reads, and it serialises the frame, because the CPU
+	// cannot begin frame N+1 until frame N's GPU work has finished.
+	//
+	// Measured on RK3588: 17 ms of a 25 ms frame, with the GPU idle for the remainder.
+	//
+	// This is the bgfx-side counterpart of SDL_KMSDRM_SKIP_EGL_SURFACE, which already stops SDL owning
+	// presentation for this surface. Runtime rather than compile time, so the first frames (before the
+	// embedder's buffers exist) and any fallback still present normally.
+	bool s_skipPrimarySwap = false;
+
 	void GlContext::swap(SwapChainGL* _swapChain)
 	{
 		makeCurrent(_swapChain);
 
 		if (NULL == _swapChain)
 		{
-			if (NULL != m_display)
+			if (NULL != m_display && !s_skipPrimarySwap)
 			{
 				EGL_CHECK(eglSwapBuffers(m_display, m_surface) );
 			}
@@ -880,5 +895,12 @@
 
 } /* namespace gl */ } // namespace bgfx
 
+// FORK PATCH (4kp): see s_skipPrimarySwap above. C linkage so the embedder can flip it without
+// linking against bgfx internals.
+extern "C" void bgfx_set_skip_primary_swap(bool _skip)
+{
+	bgfx::gl::s_skipPrimarySwap = _skip;
+}
